  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to a **GMAT Sentence Correction question**! Here is a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcdd GMAT Sentence Correction Question\n\n**Full sentence:**\n\"Unable to build nests or care for their young, a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including warblers, vireos, flycatchers, and thrushes.\"\n\n---\n\n### Answer Choices:\n\n- **A.** a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **B.** a female cowbird will use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **C.** female cowbirds use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **D.** female cowbirds lay up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **E.** up to 40 eggs a year are laid by female cowbirds in the nests of other birds, including\n\n\n\u2705 **Correct Answer: D**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd0d Explanation:\n\n**Why A and B are wrong:**\nIn A and B, *their* (plural) does not agree with *a female cowbird* (singular).\n\n**Why C is wrong:**\nIn C, \"female cowbirds...lay up to 40 eggs a year, **including those of** warblers\" \u2014 here, *those* seems to refer to eggs, yielding the meaning that female cowbirds lay the eggs *of* warblers, which is incorrect.\n\n**Why E is wrong:**\nE is out due to incorrect modification. The opening modifier \"Unable to build nests or care for their young\" must directly modify the subject performing the action, but in E, the subject becomes \"eggs\" (passive construction), which makes no logical sense.\n\n**Why D is correct:**\nThe first major problem is the modifier \"Unable to build nests or care for their young.\" This modifier must be followed by *female cowbirds*. Notice that the modifier says \"care for **their** young,\" so it needs the **plural** form of cowbird. Option D correctly uses \"female cowbirds\" (plural) immediately after the modifier, ensuring proper modifier placement and pronoun agreement.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Key Grammar Concept: **Dangling/Misplaced Modifier**\nThe opening participial phrase **\"Unable to build nests or care for their young\"** must logically and grammatically refer to the **subject** of the main clause. Since the pronoun *their* is plural, the subject must also be plural \u2014 making **\"female cowbirds\"** the only correct choice.",
